Z||000000||Songman||03-14-2001||11:14 PM||||Okay.. I'm having a brain seizure... I know this but can't think of it for anything...<P>I need to turn off some of the background things that load in Windows because I am using like 68% before I ever start an application... What is the Run command to get to this?<P>It should be the same in any version I guess, but I am using 2000 if you think it matters.<P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Galen||03-14-2001||11:19 PM||||msconfig.exe ?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Loki||03-14-2001||11:20 PM||||Yup goto run and type in msconfig and hit enter....<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
