Z||000004||Songman||03-15-2001||11:17 AM||||Uh-oh.. no msconfig.exe in Windows 2000...<P>Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||03-15-2001||09:35 PM||||I don't know much about 2000 but I'll take a stab anyway under the assumption it's a lot like 95/98/NT4. <P>A couple of questions... What are you trying to not run? What are you talking about that's at 68%?<P>My first thought would be to run regedit from the run command. Look in HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run. The strings listed here get run when windows is rebooted (logoff and logon as a different user may do it too, it does in NT). To not run something just delete the string.<P>You should export that branch of the registry to a .reg file before deleting anything (under the file menu). That way you can put everything back if you need to by doubleclicking the file you export.<P>CAUTION: be careful in regedit you can make Windows unbootable without doing very much... ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||03-16-2001||10:45 AM||||DRH--If you right click on the My Computer icon, then left click on Properties, then left click on Performance, you should see what he's talking about.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wade87GT||03-16-2001||01:36 PM||||Songman,<BR>If you are using the MS Office tool bar (it's normally at the top right of your screen) it will use alot of ram. It loads the entire applications, on startup, into the ram and resides there waiting for your one-click call. If you are using Windows2000 you might need to log on to the "local machine" make some other changes. Also, right click the Start button, click explore and go to Startup. Delete the application shortcuts you don't want to start upon startup.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||03-16-2001||10:53 PM||||Thanks guys...<P>I'm still looking, The usual commands that work with 95/98 don't work with 2000. I'll figure something out. <P>It gets pretty bad when I can have one application running and get a message that I am running out of memory and need to close something! I have 128 megs of RAM.<P>The things ya'll pointed out are good. And I disabled those things long ago. Especially that Office Bar.. I hate that stupid thing..<P>Thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
